  "$comment": "The control audit record and its file, as a table BOTH runtimes are driven from (#146): tests/unit/test_audit.py and packages/server-node/test/audit.test.mjs read this file. `records` pins the canonical field order and the exact bytes each runtime serializes a record to — ASCII-only, so a non-ASCII reason is escaped identically. `chain` is the same four records hash-chained both ways, byte for byte; the key is a test value and nothing else. `verify` applies each case's `edits` to that chain (0-based line indexes; `crlf` joins the lines with CRLF; `split` makes files `a` and `b`) and states where the verifier must report a problem or a notice — the file:line a message starts with, or the whole message when it names no line — including the LIMIT cases it is documented not to catch. `config` is the OPCUA_AUDIT_* parsing, `unsafe_targets` the rules an existing audit file must pass (mode in octal, {path} is /srv/audit.jsonl), and `user_identity` what opcua_user_identity says for each OPC UA identity token.",
